  "standards_judgment": [
    "Fresh full read covers both event-plan versions and both owned-receiver versions, including the previously Spec-only precursors; no prior Spec receipt is misrepresented as Standards review.",
    "The narrow typed prepare/selection/prepared-artifact interfaces hide source generation and whole-input replay behind explicit checked boundaries. Versioned exact copies and protocol constants are deliberate content-addressed identity inputs; unsolicited refactoring would change reviewed scientific identities.",
    "Closed JSON membership, duplicate/nonfinite rejection, exact integer type checks, canonical type-sensitive nested identity, bounded physical reads, canonical no-symlink regular paths, stable nine-field metadata and final readset checks remain explicit.",
    "Complete four-header bodies and the exact choice-hook source are pinned. The rendered fragment has closed literal event grammar, thread tags, explicit critical frontiers, no callback or arbitrary C, no ownership claim/reset/hidden wait/assumption, and retains backend capacity/domain properties.",
    "The source-derived finite profile separately counts node, command, action, history, event and full uint32 independent draw resources. The node profile is a conditional model obligation rather than compiler-memory/RSS evidence. Unknown size remains represented by UINT_MAX, not a finite-size restriction.",
    "The receiver checks untouched static bookkeeping and payload initializedness before representing one separately owned abstract prestate. It supplies each ordered full-domain uint32 draw exactly once and invokes one finite trace; it grants no actual software/hardware ownership, allocation, initializedness or physical receiver authority.",
    "V4 resolves the complete selected physical entry before applying the fixed TraceUnit context family. Common trust and unrelated recorded rules survive, while the separately reviewed fixed context scope controls the SourceUnit/TraceUnit family. Caller filtering and arbitrary owner/context authority are not introduced.",
    "Current and precursor tests exercise public pure preparation, exact full-artifact regeneration and mutation refusal, resource/owner/context/physical pins, negative event properties and full draws. Current tests additionally inspect actual result, replay/origin, record and scope seams through explicit AST/mocked process boundaries; they do not claim actual verifier/native/public execution."
  ]
